  "supportBoundaries": {
    "all": "Acceptance is for the named synthetic PCAP, loopback and portable-evidence workflows. Network observations, analyst hypotheses and confirmed endpoint effects remain distinct; no malware execution or generic arbitrary exploitation is claimed.",
    "external": "Proxy/user/organizational/NAT/interface/debugger/decompiler/process/sanitizer/impact context is manually imported, hash-bound and cited. Representative synthetic artifacts qualify this interface, not automatic ingestion or authenticity/causation. Seven Pro cases use actual nonempty collector exports, exact records and saved classifications; context-only confirmed-effect notes remain analyst assertions.",
    "sensor": "Distributed collection is signed sensor-scoped offline bundle sealing/import with per-sensor keys, hash checks, private receiving storage and scoped retention pruning; not a live fleet controller or proof of NAT ownership.",
    "flow": "Counters retain source sampling/snapshot semantics; interpolated time-series rates are estimates. Missing metadata and loss are explicit. Routing interface names come from imported snapshots; zero egress remains a candidate, not proof of a drop. Recon pagination is bound to the source file hash.",
    "ftp": "Control/data attribution and file extraction are qualified after stream readers drain, across active/passive STOR/RETR. Ambiguous, protected, unrelated and unsupported endpoints are reported rather than guessed; this is not live pre-drain extraction.",
    "protocol": "Active experiments are session-bounded against owned loopback fixtures, with finite frames/bytes/time and explicit reset/control observations. UDP server emulation is single-peer; foreign peers and oversized datagrams fail. Proxy injection is an explicitly framed message, and dependent-field repair covers the supported length prefix.",
    "grammar": "Analyst-declared fixed/variable fields and definite-length TLVs only, with finite depth/entry/value limits and strict frame consumption. Interpretation is a hypothesis, not automatic protocol discovery; grammar generation remains limited to supported fixed layouts.",
    "resources": "Finite target work counters, expansion, nesting and file readback qualify resource/injection boundaries. Target rejection, harness timeout and harness budget stop are distinct. No general OS CPU quota, destructive exhaustion or arbitrary-target vulnerability claim.",
    "tls": "Explicit trust/hostname/pin/mTLS tests and two-leg termination are separate from ciphertext passthrough. TLS 1.2/1.3 capture plaintext requires installed tshark, matching supplied key logs and available records; result metadata hashes keys rather than returning secrets.",
    "triage": "Versioned byte/field/state mutations, supported grammar generation, reset, reproduction/minimization and hashed external reports are qualified. Process/crash/sanitizer/impact imports retain impact-unverified classification; import alone never demonstrates exploitation."
  },
